# Unit-test friendly — try at the edge, test the middle

Write new `src/` so a unit test can hit the decision without a TUI, a live DB, or a host API. Failures stay local — the sidebar slot must not die. Same shape as `dry.mdc`: one exported helper, one unit file.

## Try (soft-fail)

Wrap **I/O and host calls** in `try/catch`: `fs`, JSON, SQLite, `api.client`, `api.kv`, clipboard, git spawn, toast, session switch.

- Return `null`, `[]`, a default, or a soft error string. Do not rethrow through `sidebar_content`.
- An empty `catch` is fine when the host feature is optional (`toast`, `selectSession`).
- Missing `.omo/` / bad `oes.json` / locked DB is **not** an exception — it is `present: false` or defaults.
- `try` belongs at the **edge**. Do not sprinkle it around pure helpers (`pick`, `clamp`, `packSections`, glyphs).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — throw reaches the slot
const raw = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, "utf8"))

// ✅ GOOD — try at the edge, typed fallback
function readJson(p: string): Record<string, unknown> | null {
  try {
    if (!fs.existsSync(p)) return null
    const raw = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, "utf8"))
    return raw && typeof raw === "object" && !Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : null
  } catch {
    return null
  }
}
```

## Unit-test friendly

- **Extract** parsers, clamps, glyphs, ranks, labels, and packing into **exported** functions. JSX / `monitor` / `fs.watch` stay thin wrappers.
- A branch that can be wrong (status glyph, skip rule, row budget, path fold) must be callable as `fn(input) → output` from `test/unit/<module>.test.ts`.
- Inject data (objects, stamps, fixtures). Do not hide the rule behind `useTerminalDimensions()` or a live `opencode.db`.
- Related helpers may share one unit file. Do not mount OpenTUI to prove a label or a fold.
- Prefer **pure** helpers: pass `now`, stamps, widths, and options in. Do not read `Date.now()`, `process.env`, or terminal size inside the rule.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — decision only inside JSX
<text>{status === "done" ? "✓" : "○"}</text>

// ✅ GOOD — exported, then rendered
export function workStatusGlyph(status: string): string { /* … */ }
<text>{workStatusGlyph(work.status)}</text>
```

## Do not

- Catch-and-ignore a programmer error (bad invariant). Soft-fail **I/O and hosts**, not logic bugs.
- Add a Result/Either type, a test runner, or a mock framework. `null` / defaults and `bun:test` are enough.
- Put new behaviour only in `sidebar.tsx` / `tui.tsx` / `detail.tsx` when it can live next to `layout.ts` / `omo.ts` / `pulse.ts`.
- Copy the helper into the test — import the same export (`dry.mdc`).
- Duplicate the “update tests in the same turn” rule — that is `tests-sync.mdc`. This rule is **how** the code is shaped so those tests stay cheap.
